  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is present in the verbal report — the individual notes the higher probability of getting 0 Euros in A (80%) versus B (75%), which aligns with the definition of right-skewness (more weight on unfavorable outcomes). However, the individual does not use the concept of skewness or reference it explicitly. Instead, the justification is framed in terms of preferring a higher chance of getting money (i.e., avoiding 0), which is a different reasoning path. The decision reason prefers the more right-skewed lottery (A), but the individual chooses B, which is less right-skewed. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason as defined — they did not identify or evaluate skewness as the basis for their choice. The reasoning is conceptually related but not aligned with the stated rule of the decision reason. Thus, the individual did not use the decision reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
